argon-utils (0.1.18) unstable; urgency=medium

  * lid-agent: waking the screen power-cycles the output (off, then on).
    On the ONE UP the panel goes dark with the lid below anything Linux
    reports, and the desktop left it black after the lid opened until the
    output was cycled or the console switched (T22).
  * lid-agent: the screen is woken on every opening, a shutdown cancelled
    by opening the lid included.
  * lid-agent: started outside the desktop session (e.g. from SSH), it
    finds the compositor's Wayland socket itself, so the screen still
    works; the CPU cap still needs the desktop session, by polkit.

 -- Simon Keimer <dc0sk@mailbox.org>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 16:45:00 +0200

argon-utils (0.1.17) unstable; urgency=medium

  * lid-agent: radios it turns off are recorded, by type and name, before
    they are switched; the next start turns back on whatever a killed
    agent or a poweroff with the lid shut left off. systemd-rfkill would
    otherwise carry them across the reboot, leaving Wi-Fi off for no
    visible reason.

 -- Simon Keimer <dc0sk@mailbox.org>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0200

argon-utils (0.1.16) unstable; urgency=medium

  * argonctl lid-agent, autostarted in the desktop session, acts on a
    laptop lid per the new [lid] section: "power-save" (default) turns
    the screen off while closed, optionally the Wi-Fi and Bluetooth that
    were on and the CPU frequency, and undoes exactly that when opened;
    "shutdown" raises a notification with a sound and powers off after
    shutdown_delay_s (default 1) unless the lid is opened first. It exits
    at once on a machine without a lid switch.
  * argond: SetCpuCap on D-Bus, under the new polkit action
    org.argonutils.cpu-cap, caps the CPU at its lowest frequency and puts
    the previous limit back exactly, also when argond stops. The unit
    grants argond scaling_max_freq, and nothing else under /sys.
  * oneup-takeover takes no lid action any more: logind is set to ignore
    the lid, and [lid] decides.

 -- Simon Keimer <dc0sk@mailbox.org>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200

argon-utils (0.1.15) unstable; urgency=medium

  * /usr/libexec/argon-utils/oneup-takeover LID_ACTION [--full] hands an
    Argon ONE UP's battery and lid from argononeupd to argon-utils:
    disables argononeupd, enables the lid overlay in config.txt (backed
    up), sets HandleLidSwitch=, and with --full lets argond power off.
    Everything is recorded; oneup-restore undoes it exactly. Neither runs
    on install.
  * Removing the package after a takeover runs oneup-restore first, so
    the ONE UP is not left with argononeupd disabled and no battery watch.

 -- Simon Keimer <dc0sk@mailbox.org>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:30:00 +0200

