argon-utils (0.1.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * argond.service no longer lists argononeupd.service under Conflicts=.
    Starting argond stopped the ONE UP's vendor daemon, which also holds
    the lid switch, with nothing recorded to restore it. argond already
    stays in dry run while that daemon runs; reading the fuel gauge
    alongside it is safe. A test now keeps Conflicts= equal to the UPS
    vendor units the package retires and restores.

 -- Simon Keimer <dc0sk@mailbox.org>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 01:00:00 +0200

argon-utils (0.1.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Argon ONE UP battery: with [ups] source = "oneup", argond reads the
    laptop's Cellwise CW2217 fuel gauge (reads only, identified by its
    VERSION register first) into the same battery policy, delayed
    poweroff and status file as the PWR UPS. It acts only in mode "full"
    and only while the vendor's argononeupd is not running.
  * argonctl battery: read the ONE UP's gauge by hand.
  * On the ONE UP, CanPoweroffWithWake answers "na", so the tray does not
    offer a wake the hardware cannot do.

